{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_hosting_the_calculator", "label": "Hosting the calculator", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/hosting-the-calculator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_hosting_the_calculator_invokeremote_attaches_fit", "label": "invokeRemote, not a remote declaration, attaches the invocation token", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/hosting-the-calculator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "callCalculator() used plain fetch and would have received no token; the remote needs operations: [compute]; and a process.env URL is one URL for every installation, so region pinning needs invokeRemote. Both landed."}, {"id": "docs_hosting_the_calculator_nested_tenant_claim", "label": "The tenant claim is nested at app.installationId", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/hosting-the-calculator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A flat dict.get refused 100% of genuine traffic while all twelve harness cases passed; _claim_at walks a dotted path. context.cloudId is wrong because no context is passed to invokeRemote from a backend function."}, {"id": "docs_hosting_the_calculator_clock_skew_leeway", "label": "Clock-skew leeway 30 s against a 25 s token", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/hosting-the-calculator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Doubles the replay window; recommended 5 s but deferred until a real token's lifetime is measured, because tightening on a documentation example builds a verifier that rejects real traffic at the tail."}, {"id": "docs_hosting_the_calculator_cloud_run_two_regions", "label": "Cloud Run, request-based billing, min-instances=0, two regions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/hosting-the-calculator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Not chosen on price (inside the free tier almost everywhere): chosen for genuine scale-to-zero, the container shipping unchanged (Lambda needs a WSGI adapter, one more thing to prove does no arithmetic), and two regions being two deploys because Forge does the routing."}, {"id": "docs_hosting_the_calculator_forge_token_auth_mode", "label": "SERVICE_AUTH=forge-token", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/hosting-the-calculator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Residency routing needs invokeRemote and invokeRemote attaches the FIT; the service then holds no secret at all \u2014 four public values. shared-secret is kept for tests and CI, never launched on."}, {"id": "docs_hosting_the_calculator_cost_model", "label": "Cost model: ~$0.15 to ~$3.70 a month, both regions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/hosting-the-calculator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "1 vCPU/512 MiB, concurrency 1, 0.5 s per request, 32 KB responses; egress overtakes compute at Marketplace tier; min-instances=1 costs $9.86/region/month, five times the whole bill."}, {"id": "docs_hosting_the_calculator_runners_up", "label": "Runners-up: Lambda, Fly.io, Azure Container Apps, App Runner, Fargate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/hosting-the-calculator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lambda cheapest but needs an adapter; Fly rejected on procurement not merit; Azure a coin flip; App Runner floors at $2.56/region doing nothing; Fargate disqualified structurally and deliberately not priced."}, {"id": "docs_hosting_the_calculator_realm_pinning_forge_routes", "label": "Realm pinning: Forge picks the region-specific baseUrl at install", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/hosting-the-calculator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No tenant-to-region table and no routing logic in the app, so the app can never get it wrong. operations: [compute] also declares the remote stores nothing, keeping PINNED eligibility. EU means Frankfurt or Dublin, hence europe-west3."}, {"id": "docs_hosting_the_calculator_no_ip_allowlist", "label": "No IP allow-listing", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/hosting-the-calculator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Atlassian's egress ranges carry every customer's traffic, change, and Atlassian recommends against region-specific allow-lists; the invocation token proves strictly more than an IP range."}, {"id": "docs_hosting_the_calculator_latency_budget", "label": "Latency budget: 25 s UI timeout, 5 s for triggers, FIT life 25 s", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/hosting-the-calculator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A cold start spends the token's validity; intake.sequence at 3.07 s must never sit on a scheduled trigger (5 s, four retries)."}, {"id": "docs_hosting_the_calculator_healthz_unreachable", "label": "/healthz is swallowed by Google's front end; the deploy probes /v1/meta for a 401", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/hosting-the-calculator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Presented as a dead service on first deploy; a 401 on /v1/meta proves routing, the container and that authentication is on, which an open health endpoint cannot."}, {"id": "docs_hosting_the_calculator_cold_start_measured", "label": "Cold start measured: 1.15 s US, 0.39 s EU", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/hosting-the-calculator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One observation each; rules out the failure that mattered (token expiring before the answer) and keeps min-instances=0."}, {"id": "docs_hosting_the_calculator_weekly_rebuild_deploys", "label": "Weekly rebuild that also deploys, Mondays 03:00 UTC", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/hosting-the-calculator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The attack surface is the base image, which ages on its own schedule; a rebuild that never ships is theatre."}, {"id": "docs_hosting_the_calculator_scan_policy_actionability", "label": "Scan policy: fixable HIGH/CRITICAL block, unfixable are printed", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/hosting-the-calculator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The line is actionability not severity: blocking on unfixable findings converts the gate into an obstacle people bypass. Both Trivy passes run so --ignore-unfixed is not a silent cap. On 2026-08-28 one fixable OpenSSL CVE blocked every push, correctly."}, {"id": "docs_hosting_the_calculator_observability_no_content", "label": "Access log records counts and the installation ARI, never content", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/hosting-the-calculator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An access log holding issue keys is a copy of the customer's backlog in a log aggregator; 30-day retention, no sink, alert on 5xx only."}, {"id": "docs_hosting_the_calculator_forecast_slice_in_selection_py", "label": "The forecast slice moved into agent/tools/selection.py", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/hosting-the-calculator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "team_slice lived only in serve_live.py and the Dockerfile could not reach it; reimplementing it in JavaScript would be the second implementation ADRs 0005 and 0008 refuse. Passing the whole board to /v1/forecast makes remaining the entire backlog under a sprint caption \u2014 a credible wrong number. /v1/slice returns context ids first; the suite asserts the resolver has no team comparison of its own."}, {"id": "docs_hosting_the_calculator_switchover_sequence", "label": "The switchover in order (\u00a713)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/hosting-the-calculator.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Provision, push, confirm hosting with the shared secret, lint, switch to forge-token, the atomic baseUrl commit with uninstall/install, watch the first real token, then tighten leeway. Regional forecasts byte-identical to forecast.build() across 5,825 bytes."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_hosting_the_calculator", "target": "docs_hosting_the_calculator_invokeremote_attaches_fit", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/hosting-the-calculator.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_hosting_the_calculator", "target": "docs_hosting_the_calculator_nested_tenant_claim", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/hosting-the-calculator.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_hosting_the_calculator", "target": "docs_hosting_the_calculator_clock_skew_leeway", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/hosting-the-calculator.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, 